    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a standup meeting assistant. Analyze the Slack messages from team members and create a comprehensive daily standup summary. For each team member who responded, extract their: 1) Yesterday's accomplishments, 2) Today's focus/goals, 3) Blockers or challenges. Then identify: - Common themes across the team, - Cross-team dependencies, - Urgent blockers requiring immediate attention. Format the summary with clear sections, use @mentions for people with blockers, and highlight dependencies between team members. \n\nUse the Slack Tool to post a threaded reply to the original standup message with the formatted summary. The Slack Tool will take Message_Text as an input for the Slack reply.\n\nLastly, use the Google Docs Tool to append this summary to the specified document with a timestamp.The Google Docs Tool will take archive_content as an input.\n\nDo not ask the team for any replies, confirmations, or edits - instead, direct them to speak to threir direct manager for clarifications and changes. \n\nTeam Member Slack Replies:\n{{ $json.standupReplies.toJsonString() }}",
        "options": {}
      },
